================================================================================
Skull microCT specimens
================================================================================
  Mouse — Adult dry skull, SkyScan 1272, 6.127 um iso.
    M. Maga and collaborators, SCRI Bone and Skeletal Mechanics Lab,
    University of Washington.  License: open (terms unstated).

  Macaque — Adult Macaca mulatta dry skull, AMNH:Mammals:M-87264 (MorphoSource).
    L. E. Copes, L. A. B. Lucas, J. O. Thostenson, H. E. Hoekstra, D. M. Boyer.
    "A collection of non-human primate computed tomography scans housed in
    MorphoSource." Sci. Data 3:160001 (2016).  doi:10.1038/sdata.2016.1
    License: CC BY-NC (NON-COMMERCIAL).

  Human ("Halle") — Ex vivo adult human skull microCT, released by a third party.
    T. Kirchner. "A micro-CT of a human skull." Zenodo (2022).
    doi:10.5281/zenodo.6108435   License: open (FAIR).
    Body-donor skull, Institute of Anatomy, Martin-Luther-Universitat
    Halle-Wittenberg.

  Rat — Adult Rattus norvegicus dry skull, TMM M-2272, 29.6 um iso.
    T. B. Rowe and J. A. Maisano. "Rattus norvegicus (TMM M-2272)," Digital
    Morphology Library (DigiMorph), University of Texas at Austin.
    License: DigiMorph terms (educational/research use).

================================================================================
Brain atlases, templates & parcellations
================================================================================

Mouse
  Allen Mouse Brain CCFv3 — 25 um average template + structure annotation.
    Q. Wang, S.-L. Ding, Y. Li, et al. "The Allen Mouse Brain Common Coordinate
    Framework: A 3D Reference Atlas." Cell 181(4):936-953.e20 (2020).
    doi:10.1016/j.cell.2020.04.007   License: open (Allen Brain Atlas terms).

Macaque — NMT v2.0 symmetric template + parcellations (NIMH/AFNI public)
  NMT v2.0 template & CHARM cortical hierarchy —
    B. Jung, P. A. Taylor, J. S. Seidlitz, et al. "A comprehensive macaque fMRI
    pipeline and hierarchical atlas." NeuroImage 235:117997 (2021).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2021.117997
  SARM subcortical hierarchy —
    R. Hartig, D. Glen, B. Jung, N. K. Logothetis, G. Paxinos, et al. "The
    Subcortical Atlas of the Rhesus Macaque (SARM) for neuroimaging."
    NeuroImage 235:117996 (2021).  doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2021.117996
  D99 v2 atlas —
    K. S. Saleem, N. Logothetis. "A Combined MRI and Histology Atlas of the
    Rhesus Monkey Brain in Stereotaxic Coordinates," 2nd ed., Academic Press
    (2012); NMT-aligned release in Jung et al. (2021).

Human — MNI152 space
  MNI152 ICBM 2009a symmetric T1 template —
    V. Fonov, A. C. Evans, K. Botteron, et al. "Unbiased average age-appropriate
    atlases for pediatric studies." NeuroImage 54(1):313-327 (2011).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2010.07.033   License: open (MNI/McGill).
  Harvard-Oxford cortical + subcortical structural atlas (FSL) —
    Ships with FSL.  License: FSL license (NON-COMMERCIAL, open).
  Schaefer 2018 cortical parcellation (400 parcels, 7 networks) —
    A. Schaefer, R. Kong, E. M. Gordon, et al. "Local-global parcellation of the
    human cerebral cortex from intrinsic functional connectivity MRI."
    Cerebral Cortex 28(9):3095-3114 (2018).  doi:10.1093/cercor/bhx179
    License: MIT (CBIG).
  AAL (Automated Anatomical Labeling) —
    N. Tzourio-Mazoyer, B. Landeau, D. Papathanassiou, et al. NeuroImage
    15(1):273-289 (2002).  doi:10.1006/nimg.2001.0978   License: open (CNRS).
  Yeo 2011 7-network resting-state parcellation —
    B. T. T. Yeo, F. M. Krienen, J. Sepulcre, et al. "The organization of the
    human cerebral cortex estimated by intrinsic functional connectivity."
    J. Neurophysiol. 106(3):1125-1165 (2011).  doi:10.1152/jn.00338.2011
    License: open (FreeSurfer).
  Pauli 2018 deterministic subcortical atlas —
    W. M. Pauli, A. N. Nili, J. M. Tyszka. "A high-resolution probabilistic in
    vivo atlas of human subcortical brain nuclei." Sci. Data 5:180063 (2018).
    doi:10.1038/sdata.2018.63   License: CC0.

Cerebellum — cross-species, in MNI152 space
  Diedrichsen probabilistic cerebellar atlas (lobules + deep cerebellar nuclei) —
    J. Diedrichsen, S. Maderwald, M. Kuper, M. Thurling, K. Rabe, E. R.
    Gizewski, M. Ladd, D. Timmann. "Imaging the deep cerebellar nuclei: A
    probabilistic atlas and normalization procedure." NeuroImage 54(3):1786-1794
    (2011).  doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2011.02.009
    Lobules: J. Diedrichsen, J. H. Balsters, J. Flavell, E. Cussans, N. Ramnani.
    "A probabilistic atlas of the human cerebellum." NeuroImage 46(1):39-46
    (2009).   License: open (terms unstated).

Rat — Waxholm Space, Sprague Dawley
  WHS SD rat T2*-weighted template (39 um) —
    E. A. Papp, T. B. Leergaard, E. Calabrese, G. A. Johnson, J. G. Bjaalie.
    "Waxholm Space atlas of the Sprague Dawley rat brain." NeuroImage
    97:374-386 (2014).  doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2014.04.001   License: CC BY 4.0.
  WHS SD rat atlas v4.01 (222 structures) —
    I. E. Kleven, T. B. Leergaard, et al. "Waxholm Space atlas of the rat brain:
    a 3D atlas supporting data analysis and integration." Nature Methods
    20(11):1822-1829 (2023).  doi:10.1038/s41592-023-02034-3   License: CC BY 4.0.

